# SRG-APP-000365-AU-000210  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to perform audit reduction that
# supports after-the-fact investigations of security incidents.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000365-AU-000210
group:           V-206498
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-001877
control_rev5:    AU-7

contribution:    After-the-fact investigation needs the records to still be reachable, so
                 the application's share is the retention period it holds indexed data for
                 before rolling it to frozen.

governs:         indexes.conf - The indexes data is stored in, how large they may grow and how long data
                 is kept.

check:           indexes.conf [<index name>] frozenTimePeriodInSecs present

external:        Thawing archived buckets back into a searchable index, an operator
                 procedure outside the product's configuration
external:        The medium that holds any frozen archive, and the organization's
                 investigation procedure itself

citation:        coldToFrozenDir non_empty is removed: indexes.conf.spec:792-802 presents
                 the archive destination as one alternative to a script, nothing in the
                 check text or the fix text requires an archive, and the condition failed a
                 stock install. It also contradicted this criterion's own external
                 dependency, which already assigns thawing and the archive medium to an
                 operator procedure - a condition and an external dependency over the same
                 thing is how a checklist charges the application twice for one objective.
finding:         The application does not express a retention period for indexed records,
                 so there is no configured basis for the records remaining reachable for
                 after-the-fact investigation.
